    },
    "description": "Doodad Search's showing step: writes search.json (when given) and builds index.html beside it, the page of candidates the author picks from. search.json is { title (the object), mission? (the Mission's folder name), parts: [{ name, readsAs (what the Search Part has to read as to the player), queries (the search_doodads queries run: words and facets), candidates (ranked, best first, at most ten: { id, note (why it fits or falls short), judgedFrom: sheet | image | render | none, variation? (the variation recommended, 00 when left out), variationsChecked?: [{ variation, note? }] }), alsoConsidered: [{ id, reason }], shortlist? (the Doodad Finder's ticked ids, best first, not yet judged: [{ id, level: 0-3 (the ranker's Score), ranker: jev }]), asks? (the asks made in the Doodad Finder or with find_doodads: [{ text, tags: [{ facet, value, pinned? }], ranker? (absent when the ask was only narrowed) }]) }] }. candidates may be empty while a part has a shortlist. It refuses to build while any part's shortlist has ids in it, and names those parts: judge each shortlisted id from its picture into a candidate or alsoConsidered, empty the shortlist, and keep the asks. The page has a section per Search Part with a card per candidate (picture, name, id, size, the dependency it needs and whether the Mission has it, note, variation count, the variation its picture shows), the also-considered list folded, and a pointer to drafting a Doodad Composite. A candidate's chosen variation is pictured from the search folder's renders/ (its <id>_<variation>.jpg sheet, else its first render), else the card shows the catalog's picture and says the chosen one isn't pictured. Pictures are referenced where they are (a sheet's file URL, a gallery picture's URL), never copied. The folder is the one given, else from the slug: missions/<id>/output/doodad-search/<slug>/ for a Mission (git-ignored), or $SC2_RESEARCH_DIR/doodad-search/<slug>/ for none (an error when SC2_RESEARCH_DIR isn't set). Rebuild from search.json with the same slug and mission, or the folder. It reports the candidates whose four renders are on this machine but whose turntable sheet isn't: offer to build them, then call again with buildSheets (needs ImageMagick) and judge those candidates again from their sheets.",
    "execution": {
