    },
    "description": "Writes a shot-list cutscene (a ShotCutscene JSON file: an origin and shots, each with a camera, a duration and any backdrop actors), or one of the Mission's Cinematics (its cinematics/<id>.json, with its sets and the scene's lines; a Cinematic plays in a full-screen dialog, and the reply warns about what it films (a Set imported from a story package's cutscene, a cast model or a Light) that the map's dependencies don't load, naming the dependency to add; one the Blueprint doesn't list is a test Cinematic, written silent under name, its id by default, and named after the Cinematic the mission start cue plays it takes that one's place; a shot list is refused the name of a Cinematic the map plays), into a Mission's Map Package, at Base.SC2Data/Cutscenes/<name>.SC2Cutscene, where the Cutscene Editor opens it and the game can play it over the map's own set. With play, it also plays in a loop from map start at the shot list's origin, each run pausing AI time and skippable with Escape (a Cinematic whose scene is cued at missionStart already plays from that cue, so it gets no loop), and the map is played in the game through the Editor's Test Document, or the reply gives the author the steps when the machine's Host Adapter can't. Ask the author to close the map in the Editor first. Run compile_map first: compiling the map again keeps a shot-list cutscene, which the compile record doesn't list, and drops its play-from-start test loop; the Cinematics the Blueprint lists are written by the compile itself.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
