  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Contributes the Workspace's game-doodad notes (doodad-notes.json) to the public sc2-asset-catalog by pull request: on a new branch off origin/main, in the sc2-asset-catalog checkout named or else a fresh clone with gh, adds each doodad's Doodad Uses to its own file under packages/sc2-asset-catalog/data/doodad-uses/doodads/<id>.json (after the file's own; a use the file has already, case and spacing aside, gets the variation and scale the note adds, and is left out when it has them) and a corrected look to packages/sc2-asset-catalog/data/doodad-descriptions.json in place of its description's look, adds a changeset, commits, pushes and opens a pull request on TeamAntioch/sc2-asset-catalog with gh. Ask the author first, and show them a dry run. Kept in the Workspace, with why: Campaign Mod doodads' notes (their Doodad Uses live in the mod's doodad index), terrain objects' (sc2-adjutant's own catalog), those of a doodad sc2-asset-catalog hasn't described, and any note that names one of the Workspace's Missions, its Campaign, its mods or its characters (reword it in general words first). Contributed notes stay in the Workspace, laid over the package's uses, until a release of the package holds them, when the next add_doodad_note or contribution drops them. While one of the author's earlier contribution pull requests is still open it opens none, so the same notes don't go twice. Without gh or GitHub access it leaves the checkout as it is, keeps the notes and says so. On success a checkout goes back to its own branch, and a clone is removed. Refuses a checkout with uncommitted changes, or whose origin isn't TeamAntioch/sc2-asset-catalog.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "checkout": {
          "description": "A checkout of sc2-asset-catalog to branch in (such as the one beside the sc2-adjutant checkout): absolute, or relative to the Workspace's root. Without one, a fresh clone in a temporary folder",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "dryRun": {
          "description": "Say what would be contributed, from the checkout as it stands (or a fresh clone), and change nothing",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "workspace": {
          "description": "The Workspace this call is about, when it isn't the one the session is in: its folder, a git worktree of it, or any folder inside either (such as a Mission's), absolute. The nearest folder at or above it that holds the Workspace config serves, so a Mission that exists only in a worktree is read and written there, not in the main checkout. Without it the session's working folder serves (the MCP roots), else the Workspace the server started with",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
