  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Writes Kept whole files of a Workspace mod into its Mod Blueprint's files (ADR-0011): each copied into the mod's folder at its path in the package less Base.SC2Data/ (scripts/… for Base.SC2Data/scripts/…), which the Blueprint then owns. Without paths it takes every Kept Galaxy script, UI layout (.SC2Layout) and font style (.SC2Style). A file the Blueprint already writes (in files, as its library's Galaxy or as an Asset Source) stays as it is; a package file the compile generates, a GameData catalog, a strings file and Triggers are refused, since they're owned by their parts. Each file takes the strings it names as @<key> (a UI layout's <Text val="@UI/…"/>) into its strings, by the strings file the package has each in, from the Kept strings or the Blueprint's raw strings, which it leaves; a file the Blueprint already writes takes those it didn't then, and one removals names stays removed. Nothing in the package changes: compile_mod then writes them over their Kept originals under the Equivalence Check.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
