  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Edits Kept Content in the Mission's own Map Package (ADR-0010), changing only the elements it touches in Objects and Regions, so every other byte stays as the Editor wrote it. Doodads: move, rotate, tilt, scale, tint (null clears it), swap (type, variation), add (with at.z, or like: a doodad whose height and flags it takes) and remove. Units, points and cameras: move (a camera's target moves with it), rotate (a camera's yaw too), rename (points and cameras) and flags (set or clear Editor flags, such as UnitHidden). Regions: move, resize about the centre of their bounds, and redraw with new shapes. An object is named by its Editor Id, or a Kept unit, point or camera by its Kept Reference id; a region by its id or Kept Reference id. Angles are degrees. The edits apply in order, and all are checked before anything is written: one that names Compiled Content (on the compile record) is refused with the Blueprint field to change instead, and nothing is written while the Editor has the map open (when the Host Adapter can tell). A moved doodad keeps its height unless given z.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
