    "description": "Brings the Workspace's Campaign Mod doodad index (mods/<id>/doodad-catalog.json, ADR-0017) up to date with the mod, so its doodads are searched and pictured like the game's: each of the mod's doodads (and a game doodad only when the mod changes its model) that is new, whose model changed, whose last render failed or whose sheet isn't on this machine is rendered through the Host Adapter with the Workspace's mod packages, gets a 2×2 turntable sheet (committed under catalog-sheets/doodads/ when its model is the Workspace's own, git-ignored under catalog-sheets/game-models/ when it is the game's) and an entry with its model, the model's hash and bounds. Entries for doodads the mod no longer has are dropped. Descriptions are yours to write next: read each pending doodad's sheet and write its description into its entry in core's words, with described: "agent" (docs/reference/mod-doodad-index.md); an unpictured one from its data (name, categories, model). An author-confirmed description (described: "author") is never changed. Returns what it rendered, what has no model to draw, what failed (tried again next run) and the pending entries.",
