    "description": "Records models' animations, with each one's length and move speed, so a Cinematic can cast them: a speaking cast member's model must be recorded, or the compile refuses it. Each model goes in its owner's file (ADR-0026): a game model in model-anims.json at the Workspace root, the Campaign Mod's own model in mods/<id>/model-anims.json, and, with mission, that Mission's own model (a CModel in its Map Package's Kept data) in missions/<id>/model-anims.json. Entries already in a file are kept, and a model recorded again is replaced. A game model is exported through the Host Adapter's model.export, with the game's ModelData from the machine's cacheDir (downloaded once). A model from the Workspace's packages (its mods' and, with mission, that Mission's Map Package) is read from the package, needing neither. While the Campaign Mod's catalog or the Mission's compile record doesn't read, nothing is recorded, since which models are their own can't be told. Returns each file written with its models, each model that failed and why, and stock: the game models recorded that core's data/model-anims.json doesn't record. When stock isn't empty, offer the mapper a Missing-Feature Report (the report-missing-feature skill), once per session for all of them, so the author can add them to core for everyone.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
