  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    "description": "Reports what each texture slot of a Mission's Map Package paints, read from the package (ADR-0016): for each texture set (one per 8×8-cell block) and each of its 8 slots, the texture, the cells it is the dominant texture of, by Zone (a generating Zone's own cells, else the Kept Zone whose polygon holds them, else "(no Zone)"), and the cells with any weight of it; which slots are empty or painted nowhere; and how many more different textures fit under the Editor's 16. With a proposal (textures and the generating Zones it would paint, or set: the id of one of the Blueprint's textureSets), also: which of its textures the map has already (they cost nothing towards the 16), which are new, whether it fits, which layers the Kept ground in its Zones' blocks uses (the set must hold those textures on those layers, or the compile refuses), a slot order that meets them, which slots only those Zones use (emptying them after the move frees room), and textures that would meet themselves across the set's boundary, whatever their slots. It also lists each stretch of boundary between texture sets that needs cover, as a run of cells along an 8-cell block edge with the set and texture on each side: a hard cut where different textures meet, an artifact where a texture meets itself (whatever slot it has in each set); stretches under a cliff are left out. With render: true, it shows them over the ground round them, as the paint brushes' renders do (hard cuts red, artifacts magenta, cliff cells darkened): one image to each cluster of stretches, so sets far apart each get a readable view, with the cells each image shows. Reads only.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "mission": {
          "description": "The Mission's folder name in the Workspace's missions folder",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "proposal": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A texture set to try: textures and the generating Zones it would paint, or one of the Blueprint's textureSets",
          "properties": {
            "set": {
              "description": "One of the Blueprint's textureSets, by id, for its textures and Zones",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "textures": {
              "description": "The proposed set's textures, in slot order",
              "items": {
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
