  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Writes one of the Mission Blueprint's own triggers (ADR-0026) from calls given in the Editor's terms, or rewrites the Blueprint trigger of that name (or of \`id\`, to rename it). A call is { function, library?, params?, blocks?, disabled? }: the function by its name as the Editor shows it (Periodic Event), its identifier (TriggerAddEventTimePeriodic) or <library>/<id>, with library (Ntve or Built-In, or map for the map's own) only when the name is ambiguous (where functions share a name, the one whose kind fits where the call stands is taken); params by parameter name (or by <library>/<id> where two share a name), each left out taking the default a new call gets in the Editor (a text's words too), null leaving it unset in a disabled statement, a list giving a parameter its template repeats (Combine Text Multiple's Text) each value; blocks by slot name (If, Then, Else), each a list of statements, in the order given. A value is a number, true/false, or a string read by the parameter's type (a preset value's name such as Game Time, the map's own too, a text's words, a String, a trigger's name, a game link's id); or { function, … } for a call's value, { preset } (a library's or the map's preset value by name or reference), { bits: [value names], preset? } for a set of bits (preset naming its bits preset type where the parameter takes any), { variable, library?, index?, member? } (a local, a Blueprint or Kept global, or a library's global, by name or reference; member a structure's member by name), { trigger }, { text }, { value?, type, gameType?, valueId?, typeInfo?, context? } for a literal as the Editor writes it (valueId a placed unit's, point's or region's number), { expression, type, slots? } for an Arithmetic or Expression value (type Integer, Real, String or Text; expression its text with ~<code>~ slots, a Text one's words; slots each code's value), { customScript, type? }. A statement is a call, { comment } or { customScript } (Galaxy text, written only where asked for); events may hold comments. The trigger is { name, id?, initiallyOff?, disabled?, identifier?, label?, section?, variables?: [{ name, type (Unit Group, or a preset type's name), value?, array?, constant?, identifier? }], events, conditions, actions }. Each value is checked against its parameter's type, and every name against the libraries in reach and the map's own; an unknown, ambiguous or wrongly typed one is refused in the Editor's terms, and nothing is written. When no game function does the job, the refusal says so: write custom script only where the mapper asks, and offer a Missing-Feature Report (report-missing-feature). outline_trigger reads a trigger back in this form, to edit and rewrite. Rewriting keeps the trigger's Id, its locals' and every unchanged call's. Writes missions/<id>/triggers/<name>.json and lists it in the Blueprint's triggers; compile_map writes it into the Map Package.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
