    "description": "Lists what the Workspace's Campaign Mod defines, as Mission compiles and the checkers read it: its tilesets (each with its blend textures, cliff sets, default Light and sky, resolved through its parents), terrain textures, cliff sets, Lights, units (whether each flies or is a structure), doodads (with their variation counts, their model files and, where the mod's doodad index (mods/<id>/doodad-catalog.json) covers them, their descriptions in core's words, who wrote each, their sheets' absolute paths when on this machine, why they have no picture, or that they're pending: index-mod-doodads renders them and an agent describes them) and models. Kept entries come from the mod's package, Blueprint-owned ones from its Mod Blueprint. The game's own entries are core's: its catalog files (packages/core/data/*-catalog.json and tileset-*.json) and the published sc2-asset-catalog's textures and cliff sets, with their extracted fields in packages/core/data/texture-extracted.json and cliff-extracted.json; a Mission uses either.",
