  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Compiles a Melee Map Blueprint (a 1v1 ladder-style map: zones, ramps, resource bases and a start base per spawn, with no Beats or Screenplay) into a Map Package the Galaxy Editor calls Melee: User players with any race and a random start, every resource base the standard ladder base, each main's ramp the diagonal ladder ramp with an unbuildable plate at its foot, a StartLoc at each start base, the stock Melee Initialization trigger and Void (Mod) as the only dependency. A melee map needs no Mission: the blueprint can be in any folder. A broken melee rule (the Editor's melee checklist, a non-standard start base, a missing symmetry partner, a main's second ground entrance, no standard main ramp, a feature TLMC forbids) fails the call, naming the rule and the object, and writes nothing. Returns where it wrote the package, any warnings from drawing it, and the distance report: worker seconds ramp to ramp, main to main, natural to natural, main to natural and to the thirds, rocks up and down, and air against ground, with a warning for each number outside the Standard bands.",
    "execution": {
