  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Compiles a Workspace mod's Mod Blueprint into its committed mod package in place (ADR-0011, under ADR-0010's compile record). Its writers replace only what compile-record.json lists and leave every Kept byte as the Editor wrote it: catalog entries by entry in their GameData files (gameData raw, and entries: generic typed entries, each checked against the game's data schema first, every problem listed by entry, as convert_entries writes them), string keys (strings: the Blueprint's raw strings, each generic entry's and character's own strings, and DocInfo/Name, DescShort and DescLong from the Blueprint's name and description), the library's functions from its interface (library: each function's FunctionDef spliced into Triggers, its strings, and a GUI function's Galaxy written into Lib<id>.galaxy as the Editor generates it, as convert_library writes them; an interface change that would renumber an id the package has fails the compile), the Campaign Mod's Screenplays (screenplays: each interlude or set of hub chats, from its pulled copy in the mod's folder, compiled into the CConversation it names, each scene a group and each line a conversation line with the naming template's line id, its imported Sound kept, its speaker's character from the Blueprint's characters, and its text and scene titles into ConversationStrings, as convert_screenplay declares them), the library's triggers and globals spliced into Triggers (triggers), files written whole (files: scripts, cutscenes, UI, plain files), a Campaign Mod's Set cutscenes (setCutscenes: each Set written back as the cutscene it names, with no shots, so its room opens in the Cutscene Editor; an Editor change to one comes back through sync_mod), a Campaign Mod's sound sets (soundSets: a CSound in SoundData for each line of a conversation, on a dialogue parent in the template form or with its AssetArray in full, a line in a form of its own if it has one, playing the voice file its Asset Mod declares for the line's Sound, as convert_sound_set writes them), and an Asset Mod's files from their Asset Sources (assets: a Workspace file checked against its SHA-256, a community asset fetched once to the machine's cache and checked against its SHA-256, a generated placeholder, or one derived from another by a named step such as wav-to-ogg; voices: a voice file per line of a Campaign Mod conversation, its recording if it has one (a recording whose file this machine doesn't have leaves the package's voice file as it is, with a warning), else a placeholder spoken in its character's voice; a community asset or placeholder is git-ignored by the mod folder's .gitignore, which the compile writes); once the Blueprint owns anything it also generates DocumentInfo (its dependencies, and preloads derived from the model, sound and texture files its entries name) and DocumentHeader with its dependencies, the ComponentList and the .version stamps. A part written over a Kept one is converted under the Equivalence Check: compared with the original as the Editor reads it (ordering, whitespace, attribute order and number formatting ignored), and any difference the Blueprint's acceptedDifferences doesn't name, with a reason, fails the compile, writing nothing, and lists each. Each of the Blueprint's removals (Accepted Removals: a Kept string:<strings file>:<key>, line:<strings file>:<text> for a line with no key, or file:<path>, with its reason) is removed from the package, and the check expects it gone: a whole strings file is compared with its original less them, and a part that writes one back fails. When the author has changed Compiled Content in the Editor since the last compile, the compile stops, writing nothing, and lists each change by entry (catalog-entry:<file>:<Class>:<id>, string:<file>:<key>, trigger:<id>, function:<id>, file:<path>): ask the author whether to keep each one (it stays as the Editor left it and leaves the record, as Kept Content) or discard it (overwritten), then compile again with keep, discard, keepAll or discardAll. Returns what it converted, any warnings, the voice files that are placeholders (each line's, and why it has no recording), and the mod's Kept report by component.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "discard": {
          "description": "Entries the compile listed as changed in the Editor to discard: overwritten with what the Blueprint says",
          "items": {
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
        "discardAll": {
          "description": "Discard every change the compile lists (an entry in keep still stays)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "keep": {
          "description": "Entries the compile listed as changed in the Editor to keep as the Editor left them (object:<id>, trigger:<id> …): each leaves the compile record, as Kept Content the Blueprint no longer writes",
          "items": {
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
        "keepAll": {
          "description": "Keep every change the compile lists (an entry in discard still goes)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "mod": {
          "description": "The mod's id, as the Workspace config's mods names it (its folder in mods/)",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "workspace": {
          "description": "The Workspace this call is about, when it isn't the one the session is in: its folder, a git worktree of it, or any folder inside either (such as a Mission's), absolute. The nearest folder at or above it that holds the Workspace config serves, so a Mission that exists only in a worktree is read and written there, not in the main checkout. Without it the session's working folder serves (the MCP roots), else the Workspace the server started with",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "mod",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
