  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Writes Kept functions of a Workspace Campaign Mod's GUI trigger library into its Mod Blueprint's library interface (ADR-0011), keeping their imported ids: each function's name, kind, parameters with their types and defaults, grammar and hint. A GUI function's body goes in library/<identifier>.json, typed calls stored as data; a native one's body is the script file in the package that defines it, copied into the mod's folder (scripts/… for Base.SC2Data/scripts/…), which the Blueprint then owns. It writes the library's other items into the interface too: its categories (trigger folders) with what each files, in order, preset types and their values, structures and their members, comments and custom script, with their names, and the Root's order the first time one converts; a category may file a Kept item, such as a trigger convert_triggers hasn't converted. A function or item stays Kept, with the reason, when its XML holds a form the conversion doesn't write yet, its Galaxy can't be written as the Editor would (a call to a function the game's libraries don't define, a template macro it doesn't know, a function that runs in its own thread), or no one script file defines a native one. Nothing in the package changes: compile_mod then writes the functions, their strings and their Galaxy over the Kept originals under the Equivalence Check.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
