  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Declares the Screenplay a Kept CConversation of a Workspace Campaign Mod comes from (an interlude or a set of hub chats) in its Mod Blueprint's screenplays (ADR-0011): it asks the Screenplay Source which Screenplay that is (or takes ref), pulls it into screenplays/<conversation>.md in the mod's folder, and keeps the imported ids. The Conversation's name (Conversation/Name/<conversation> in ObjectStrings), from the Blueprint's raw strings or the Kept ones, is recorded as the declaration's name, which the compile writes; it leaves the raw strings, and one that removals names refuses the conversion. The naming template names each line, and those must be the Conversation's line ids line for line, or it is refused, naming each line on either side; each line keeps the Sound it was imported with. A wordless scene (directions, no lines) is an empty group, and a group keeps the stale name the Editor gave it (importedGroupNames). The Conversation must then compile as the Editor has it, so what can still differ is the lines' text: each string whose Screenplay text differs from the Kept one is listed (trailing space aside, which the check ignores), to name in the Mod Blueprint's acceptedDifferences or change at the Source. Only on the author's decision: accept (the reason) lets the Conversation's groups or ids differ, recorded as its Accepted Difference, while each line must still compile as the Editor's under its Kept id; and renumber, with accept, pairs the lines of a Screenplay the author renumbered at the Source with the Conversation's in order (one for one, same speakers), keeps their Sounds under the new ids, accepts the strings the new ids collide with, and makes the mod package's Kept references follow (convline values in Triggers and Galaxy, line ids in cutscenes), listing each file. Otherwise nothing in the package changes: compile_mod then writes the Conversation and its strings over their Kept originals under the Equivalence Check. Given a Kept-terrain Mission instead of a mod (and no conversation, ref, source or renumber), it converts the Map Package's own conversation, the one the Blueprint's screenplay.script.conversationId names, to the Mission's Screenplay, pulled from the Source: it records in screenplay.script.conversion what each line keeps (a line whose words are unchanged keeps its imported Sound and recording; a changed or added line gets the naming template's Sound and a placeholder voice; a dropped line is left out), and lists every difference: changed, added and dropped lines, speaker changes, the Kept cutscene elements the compile relinks, the Sounds (with their recordings) and strings the first compile removes as nothing plays them (a Sound a Kept trigger names stays, listed apart), and each part the first compile writes other than as the Editor has it, which the Equivalence Check refuses until acceptedDifferences names it. Only on the author's decision, accept (the reason) names each of those as accepted. Nothing in the package changes: compile_map, in place, then writes the conversation over its Kept original. The result is under mission in the structured output.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "accept": {
          "description": "The author's reason the Conversation may compile other than as the Editor has it (such as the naming template's Line01001 for the Editor's Line00001), recorded as its Accepted Difference; for a Mission, each difference the first compile meets is named in acceptedDifferences with it. Only on the author's decision",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "conversation": {
          "description": "The mod's Kept CConversation id, such as HubConversation-Medic; needed with mod. A Mission's comes from its screenplay.script.conversationId",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "mission": {
          "description": "A Kept-terrain Mission whose Map Package's own conversation is converted, its folder name in the Workspace's missions folder; give this or mod",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "mod": {
          "description": "The mod's id, as the Workspace config's mods names it (its folder in mods/); give this or mission",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "ref": {
          "description": "What the Screenplay Source knows its Screenplay by, when the Source can't tell from the conversation",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "renumber": {
          "description": "The author renumbered the Screenplay at its Source on purpose: pair its lines with the Conversation's in order and make the Kept references follow the new ids; needs accept",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "source": {
          "description": "The Screenplay file in the mod's folder; screenplays/<conversation>.md when not given. Without a Screenplay Source, it must already be there",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "workspace": {
          "description": "The Workspace this call is about, when it isn't the one the session is in: its folder, a git worktree of it, or any folder inside either (such as a Mission's), absolute. The nearest folder at or above it that holds the Workspace config serves, so a Mission that exists only in a worktree is read and written there, not in the main checkout. Without it the session's working folder serves (the MCP roots), else the Workspace the server started with",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
