  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    "description": "Doodad Search's narrowing step by meaning, from the Doodad Finder (served when the doodad-finder package, an optional dependency of core, is installed). Give a Search Part's line as the ask. It narrows the same doodads search_doodads searches, with the Workspace's Doodad Uses, to about 200 candidates by keywords and a local embeddings model, so it finds what shares no word with the ask ("cover" finds sandbags and crates). Then Jev grades each candidate's text card (name, id words, look, facets, Doodad Uses) on four levels: 0 doesn't fit, 1 related but wrong, 2 could work with dressing or scale, 3 reads as exactly this. Results come best first: fit first, then a doodad the Mission's dependencies provide over one no more than 0.25 above it. Each result is search_doodads' (picture, dependency, provided, hasRenders and the rest) with its level; the answer says the ranker, how many the narrowing gave it, timings and the call's estimated spend. The ranker judges text, never pictures: judge every candidate from its picture as usual. With rank false, or with no TypeSafe key, or when Jev fails, it gives the narrowing's order and says why. Lights and other doodads with no description have only their name and id words: search_doodads finds those better. The first call loads the model, cards and vectors, which then stay loaded. Each ranked call sends the ask, the tags and the candidates' cards to TypeSafe; no pictures or files. Reads only.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "properties": {
        "ask": {
          "description": "A Search Part's line, such as "press head: a heavy flat block that drops onto a belt"",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "count": {
          "description": "At most this many results; 20 by default",
          "maximum": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "mission": {
          "description": "The Mission to mark for: the doodads its dependencies provide are kept and come first among equals",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "rank": {
          "description": "False gives the narrowing alone, with no call to the ranker; true by default",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "tags": {
