          "description": "The Workspace this call is about, when it isn't the one the session is in: its folder, a git worktree of it, or any folder inside either (such as a Mission's), absolute. The nearest folder at or above it that holds the Workspace config serves, so a Mission that exists only in a worktree is read and written there, not in the main checkout. Without it the session's working folder serves (the MCP roots), else the Workspace the server started with",
