  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    "description": "Read-only. Returns one catalog entry (a unit, ability, actor, weapon, behaviour, effect ...) as the game reads it: its definitions merged across Blizzard's data and then a mod's, in load order; the class default and parent chain it inherits; its ##token## values filled in (\`##id##\` is its own id); removed="1" elements dropped (listed apart); each field with the layer or entry it came from; and the entries that name it (as parent, a token value, or a whole attribute or text value in a field). The mod is the Campaign Mod unless \`mod\` names another Workspace mod. Blizzard's data comes from a folder laid out like SC2Mapster's SC2GameData (mods/core.sc2mod, campaigns/liberty.sc2campaign ... each with base.sc2data/GameData): give it as \`stockData\` or set SC2_ADJUTANT_STOCK_DATA; without it only the mod's own entries are read. Not checked against the Editor yet: see docs/reference/effective-entry.md.",
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden",
    },
