    "description": "Reads a Map Package compiled from a Mission and saved in the Galaxy Editor, and syncs what the author changed there back into the Blueprint: doodads moved, edited, added or deleted; units, points and cameras; regions; and on a generated map, ground raised or lowered (terrainEdits.heights), water areas drawn, moved or deleted (water pools with a rect), and the pathing brush's paint and erasing over what the compile paints under dug pools and solid doodads (pathingPaint, a stroke near a doodad kept relative to it; docs/reference/doodad-pathing.md). Cliff-level changes and texture paint are listed as not synced. In the Mission's own package only Compiled Content on its compile record comes back: an object or region the author made there is Kept Content and stays where it lies, except a doodad standing on ground the compile writes (a generating Zone's, or any Zone's on a generated map), which becomes an Anchor at its own Editor Id (editorId), so the compile takes it over where it stands. Beside Kept ground, objects and regions sync only from the Mission's own package with a compile record, against the ground and dressing the compile writes there; the Zones' hidden cells sync there too. Run it after each Editor save, before changing the Blueprint again. The Blueprint is saved only if it still validates. Editor settings the Blueprint can't keep are listed, not kept. It also copies the skills of the Plugins the Workspace lists into its .claude/skills/, as the Claude Code plugin's SessionStart hook does, so a Plugin listed since the session started brings its skills.",
