    "description": "Shows what the game's terrain textures look like, to choose them by sight rather than by name (ADR-0016, the texture-sets skill): a sheet of their pictures, each labelled with its id and its catalog look, from the sc2-mapping-reference gallery (fetched once into the machine's cache). Name the textures (CTerrainTex ids, with an optional label each, such as a role or slot), or search the catalog (the published sc2-asset-catalog's descriptions, with core's data/texture-extracted.json) by its descriptions: words any of which the look holds ("grat" finds grating), words to leave out, kind (built or natural), tones, roles the texture suits (base, path, variety, high, low, accent) and tilesets. A search returns the matches' ids and looks as text, and the first \`limit\` (default 24) on the sheet. A texture with no gallery picture shows as a grey tile: judge it from its look, or in the Editor.",
